

   =====( GraphUsage V1.00 )=========================================


           Trion GraphUsage CliDoor and/or Utility.

           (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '96-'97. All rights reserved.

           Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


        This programm will show an ANSI graph of the usage of
        the system in minutes every hour of the last couple of
        days .. like in the right bottom corner
        of the TrionRM monitor. But bigger and with information
        about the graph around it, like hours and minutes.
        And it has an indication which day the information
        is about.

        You could use it in your bulletin menu by adding something
        like the folowing:


        Cmd "U" , 0-255
           CliDoor  "doors:lastcallers/GraphUsage"
           More
        EndCmd


        Or you could call it in a script to make an ANSI screen
        that is shown when someone logs in.
        In that case you have to redirect the output to a
        file by putting a > and a file name after the
        door name at the command line like this:


        doors:lastcallers/GraphUsage >trion:text/login3.ansi


        You could add this line to the lastcaller script so
        it is called every time someone logs of or there was
        an incoming mail call.


        In the default BBS config there is a 'Lastcallers' script
        in the "Trion:scripts/" directory.
        In this script a lastcaller screen and a UsageGraph
        are made, the script itself is started from logout
        and incoming scripts.
        So if you want to change the way the UsageGraph
        programm is started you only have to change one script.


        Note that the data used for the graph comes from the
        'Trion:data/lastusers.bin' file .. if you want to use
        an other data directory then the default directory in 
        the TrionRM.cfg .. you have to give the name and path
        of the new data file on the command line of this programm.



